4. LIST OF PROJECT ASSUMPTIONS (MANDATORY REQUIREMENT 40)
---------------------------------------------------------
1. Read-Only Storage Assumption: In accordance with project rules, all market locations, schedules, and crop data are loaded from static local JSON files without backend databases.
2. Rule-Based Chatbot Assumption: The AI chatbot uses internal pattern-matching logic on a pre-scripted agricultural and navigation dataset. No external paid AI API keys are required.
3. Local/Session Persistence Assumption: Bookmarking and personal shopping notes rely on HTML5 localStorage and synchronized session state, maintaining user selections across tab refreshes without server overhead.
4. Geolocation Fallback Assumption: If browser geolocation is denied or unavailable, the application falls back gracefully to default regional distances from central Karachi without interrupting functionality.
5. Simulated Authentication Assumption: The Login and Sign Up interfaces are prototype modal forms created for design continuity and UX evaluation.
6. Real-Time Radar Assumption: Market "Open Now" status is determined dynamically by comparing the user device's local clock day and time with the market's verified weekly schedule table.

5. AI USAGE ACKNOWLEDGMENT (REQUIREMENT 43 & 44)
------------------------------------------------
AI tools (Antigravity) were utilized strictly as a supporting programming aid for code formatting, accessibility refinements, and document compilation. No unauthorized closed-source boilerplates or ready-made templates were used. All architecture decisions, dataset designs, and logic checks were directed to fulfill the project requirements.
